<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">García II of Galicia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1042">1042</a>–1090</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">García II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-leon">Ferdinand I of León</a> who received the Kingdom of Galicia, with northern Portugal, when his father's realms were divided in 1065. In 1071 his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-ii-of-castile">Sancho II of Castile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> of León deposed him. He spent most of his later life imprisoned by Alfonso and died in captivity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garcia-ii-of-galicia.jpg" alt="García II of Galicia" width="179" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alonso de Cartagena (1385?-1456) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garcia_II_of_Galicia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
